    {
      "type": "info",
      "sectionId": "info",
      "label": "about me",
      "imageId": "test-landscape.jpg",
      "text": "<p>My name is Varvara Polyakova,</p><p>I\u2019m a diverse visual artist working across the fields of graphic design, illustration and ceramics.</p><p>I graduated from the Moscow State University of Printing Arts and I'm a member of the Moscow Union of Artists (Department of Graphics) and the Tzeh illustrators community.</p><p>After completing my studies, I worked in several design studios and magazines as a graphic designer and an art director and collaborated with cultural institutions such as the Petr Fomenko Theater, the \u201c4. Block\u201d Poster festival, the Japanese Cultural Center and so on. As an editorial illustrator I've worked for a range of top magazines in Moscow.</p><p>In 2012 I moved from Moscow to Berlin and I also started creating ceramics under the brand name Palavara.</p><p>You can find my ceramic works in my Etsy shop: <a href='https://www.etsy.com/shop/PALAVARA' target='_blank'>www.etsy.com/shop/PALAVARA</a></p><p>I also teach art classes for children and offer individual pottery classes for adults.</p><p>I'd be more than happy to discuss any potential projects or collaborations.</p><br /><p>Please contact me via e-mail: <a href='mailto:varya@palavara.com'>varya@palavara.com</a></p>",
      "lqip": "data:image/jpeg;base64,"
    }
